From 78b4e80630bb0f59ad9350e4673b4c065eef0450 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:52:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(goldens): cover all seven harnesses, pin validate,
 assert the accounting contract

Sources and targets: Gemini (the 0.47 JSONL stream, assembled in-process
because the adapter's reader takes one JSON document), opencode (the
`opencode export` wrapper, translated to Session rows as the matrix test
does) and Cursor (a CursorSession document). Nine sets, six targets each:
54 projections and 54 round trips, every pair `compared`. A projection is
what `path p export <agent> -o` writes; Cursor's is pinned with keys sorted
because its composer rows carry hash maps that reorder per run, as
Copilot's is for its minted session id.

Inputs come from one place each: fixture-backed sets read
test-fixtures/<agent>/convo.* directly (the set is named after the agent);
goldens/<name>/input.* keeps claude-session (live capture) and
claude-compacted (derived). The old tool's goldens/<agent>/input.jsonl
copies are byte-identical and skipped, so the four shared sets' snapshots
are unchanged.

validate@<set>: the validation `path p validate` runs (toolpath.schema.json
plus the bundled kind schemas, by meta.kind) over the document and every
round-trip document; all valid today.

The v1.1.0 accounting contract as an invariant, asserted per set with the
differing field in the message: the token_usage of every
conversation.append step summed, the adapter's total_usage and the
extracted total_usage must agree, counters and breakdowns class by class.
Three gaps found and pinned as known defects so a fix shows as a snapshot
change: copilot (input and cache totals live only on session.shutdown),
gemini and opencode (sum_usage and accumulate_total drop per-turn
breakdowns).

json_lines becomes json_values: a whole-document input is one value, a
JSONL transcript one per line, so detection, shed and the defects measure
both shapes. qualifier records re-recorded at their new anchors, four new
concerns recorded.
